# --- Secret-shaped files (jul26) ------------------------------------------
# A live RSA private key DID reach history once: fpl26contest-key.pem, 1674 B,
# commit 4d26386 (2026-05-09, a 186-file WIP snapshot). It is gone from HEAD but
# permanent in history. These patterns stop a recurrence; they CANNOT un-commit
# the existing one — only ROTATING that key makes the historical copy inert, and
# that must happen before this repo is ever pushed to a hosted service (even a
# private one: private is not a security boundary, and GitHub secret scanning
# does not cover private repos without Advanced Security).
# scripts/build_submission.sh:60 already fails the build on these patterns.
*.pem
*.key
*_key
*credentials*
.env.*
!.env.example
